## Summary of findings

Important upfront discrepancy: The acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.java` describes an "identity-key-v2" algorithm (SHA-256 64-hex over `normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`), but the actual implementation `IdentityKey.of(...)` returns a plain, unhashed string `telephone + "|" + email` with no soundex. No soundex implementation exists anywhere in the repo (only the word appears in the test Javadoc). The `openapi.yml` DTO description also documents the plain `normalizedTelephone|email` form. So the test's `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` expectation is not met by current code.

Also note pipeline wiring: only `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity` (hard 409) and `DetectPossibleDuplicate` (soft match) are actually wired into `owners.POST.yml`. The classes `RejectDuplicateHousehold`, `RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail`, and `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone` (and their escalation YAMLs) exist but are NOT referenced in the POST pipeline.

---

## 1. Identity key, household id, duplicate detection, soft match, blocklist, soundex, telephone normalization

### Identity key
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/IdentityKey.java` — plain `telephone + "|" + email`:
```java
15	    public static String of(String telephone, String email) {
16	        return telephone + "|" + (email == null ? "" : email);
17	    }
```

### Household id
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/HouseholdId.java` — first 12 hex chars (6 bytes) of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName)+"|"+normalize(postcode)`:
```java
19	    public static String of(String lastName, String postcode) {
20	        String key = normalize(lastName) + "|" + normalize(postcode);
21	        try {
22	            byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(key.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
23	            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
24	            for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
25	                sb.append(String.format("%02x", digest[i]));
26	            }
27	            return sb.toString();
28	        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
29	            throw new IllegalStateException(e);
30	        }
31	    }
33	    private static String normalize(String value) {
34	        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
35	    }
```
Note: HouseholdId keys off postcode (not `address`), though the Javadoc/openapi say "address". Household cap and gold-tier logic in `HouseholdCap.java` and `HouseholdTier.java` (both full contents captured above) also key off `HouseholdId.of(lastName, postcode)`.

